e during 2026 |\n| pt-0023 Burma Leuschke | 46 (turns 46 on 2026-12-15) | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0005) and message sent (comm-t0011) | In the population; no screening on record |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver | 51 | Open gap: no new order | Stool blood test on 2024-06-11, outside the 2026 window. She already has an active FIT order from 2026-09-30 (sr-t3-6648); the policy forbids a duplicate |\n| pt-0025 Danika Ullrich | 51 | Screening up to date | Normal CT colonography on 2022-03-08 (proc-t3-5032), inside the 4-year lookback (2022–2026) |\n| pt-0034 Rickey Sipes | 72 | Excluded | Age 66 or older and living long term in a nursing home: his home address is Maple Grove Care Center, Room 214, with nursing facility visits in 2026-02 and 2026-07 after a 2025-12 stroke |\n| pt-0035 Elvin Wolff | 68 | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0006) and message sent (comm-t0012) | No screening on record. His May 2026 nursing facility stay was short-term rehab after a hip fracture, and he went home, so the nursing home exclusion does not apply |\n\nTotals: 2 up to date, 7 open gaps (6 newly ordered, 1 already had an active order), 4 excluded, 1 not in population.\n\nTwo points for you to check:\n- **pt-0024:** I sent no outreach message. The policy ties the message to a new order, and I found no record of a patient message about the existing September order. You may want a reminder sent to her.\n- **pt-0022:** Her FIT result was negative in December 2025. The kit fills the 2026 measure gap, but clinically her next annual test is not due until December 2026.",
